  "description": [
    "`a % b` keeps the width and takes the dividend's sign (`-7 % 2` is -1, `7 % -2` is 1): `division_type: TRUNCATE`. `pmod(a, b)` is the floored remainder (`pmod(-7, 2)` is 1, `pmod(-7, -2)` is -1).",
    "`MIN % -1` is 0 at every width, in both modes; `%` never overflows. A zero divisor raises `REMAINDER_BY_ZERO` under ANSI and gives NULL without it."
  ],
  "reference": "`modulus` with `division_type: TRUNCATE` (the remainder has the dividend's sign), `on_division_by_zero: ERROR` when omitted, `MIN % -1` is 0 (`min_mod_neg_one`), no overflow. Spark's `%` under ANSI is native.",
  "status": "no-finding",
  "evidence": "probe",
